<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-determinants" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Determinants</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      The determinant condenses a square matrix into a single number that decides
      invertibility. We define it by cofactor expansion, learn how row operations change
      it <mdash /> which makes it computable by row reduction <mdash /> and then establish
      how it interacts with inverses, products, and transposes. The chapter closes with
      the determinant's geometric meaning: it measures volume, and tells us how a linear
      transformation scales it.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="determinants/sec-cofactor-expansion.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="determinants/sec-determinants-row-operations.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="determinants/sec-determinants-inverses-products.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="determinants/sec-determinant-volume.ptx" />
</chapter>
